WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.230
In October 2015, large shops
in England began charging

2
00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:06.850
5 pence for a plastic bag.

3
00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:10.440
In 2021, the charge doubled to 10 pence,

4
00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:12.420
and spread to all shops.

5
00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:13.990
A tiny price.

6
00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:16.460
But it points to a giant question.

7
00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:18.790
Economies keep producing more.

8
00:00:18.790 --> 00:00:22.940
Can that go on without using up
what the next generation will need?

9
00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:25.860
In this mission, you'll meet
the government's toolkit,

10
00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:29.850
from taxes to pollution permits
that firms can buy and sell.

11
00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:34.390
Then you'll weigh the benefits of
growth against its costs to the planet.

12
00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:37.380
Your mission: find out
whether growth and a cleaner

13
00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:39.000
planet can go together.
